messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/vms_term_sock.c
Line: 163
Function: main
Bug type: stack-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-121
Explanation: After recv, the code writes a NUL terminator at TermBuff[len] without validating len. If recv returns -1 (error), this writes before the buffer; if it returns sizeof(TermBuff) (80), it writes one byte past the end, causing a stack-based out-of-bounds write.

